course: dictionary
lesson: 2347
title: Crybaby: a word that can hurt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A crybaby is someone who cries or complains easily over small things. It is an informal word, and it is unkind when you say it to someone else.
explain: «Don't be a crybaby» is often said to tease someone. Everyone cries sometimes, so the name can hurt a friend who is already upset. Before you use a word like this, ask how it will make the other person feel.
explain: Context shows you how a word is used. «He called him a crybaby» tells you the boy was being teased for crying. The sentence does not mean the boy was a real baby, and the teasing is the important clue.
fact: Crybaby is a noun. You can have one crybaby or many crybabies, and it is also written as cry-baby.
fact: «Crybaby» means someone, especially a child, who cries or complains easily over small things.
fact: «Crybaby» can also mean an adult who moans when things do not go their way.
fact: Crybaby is informal and unkind, so it is not a polite word to call a friend.
fact: In Russian, «plaksa» means crybaby, and «ne plAch» means «don't cry», which is said to comfort a smaller child.
exercise: What does crybaby mean? | A baby who is very quiet and calm | A kind friend who helps you when you are sad | *Someone who cries or complains easily over small things
exercise: «Calling a crying friend a crybaby is never fair.» Why can this be unkind? | *It shows your friend is the strongest in class | Everyone cries sometimes, and the name hurts a friend who is upset | It means your friend is a real baby | It is a polite way to say hello
exercise: Which person could be called a crybaby in the dictionary sense? | A child who laughs at a joke | A dog that wags its tail | A teacher who reads a story | *An adult who moans every time things do not go their way
test: Which word is informal and unkind when used for someone who cries easily? | gentle | polite | kind | *crybaby
test: Which sentence is the kindest thing to say to a crying friend? | «Calm down, you are such a crybaby» | *«Don't cry, I am here with you» | «Only babies cry» | «Stop being a crybaby»
exam: Why can calling someone a crybaby be unkind? | It is always a fair thing to say | It means they are older than you | It is a funny joke that everyone enjoys | *It hurts, because everyone cries sometimes and an upset friend needs help, not a name
